const PRIVACY = "**Effective Date: November 16, 2026**\n\n**Operator**\n\nEthan Martin\n\n**Support**\n\nethanmartin95@hotmail.com\n\n## Scope\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how the mobile application (the “App” or the “Application”) operated by Ethan Martin (“we,” “us,” or “our”) handles information when you use its AI-assisted video, image, prompt-building, chat, library, export, and subscription features.\n\nThe App does not require account registration or login. We do not operate a user-content backend, use Firebase, run advertising analytics, or use a third-party crash-reporting or diagnostics service in the current version.\n\n## Information Processed by the App\n\nDepending on the feature you choose, the App may process:\n\n- text prompts, Prompt Builder inputs, and AI chat messages;\n- chat context needed to continue a conversation thread;\n- images you select from Photos or capture with the camera for chat, image generation, or image-to-video generation;\n- images generated within AI chat and reused as source material for animation or video generation;\n- generated images and videos stored in the App’s local library;\n- local chat-thread history and Prompt Builder history;\n- subscription status and purchase-related information necessary to provide paid access.\n\nWe do not ask you to create an account and do not intentionally collect your email address, advertising identifier, or general device identifier for our own analytics or advertising purposes. Network and service providers may process technical connection information, such as IP address or request metadata, under their own policies when your device communicates with them.\n\n## Brand Name and Trademark Authorization\n\n**Signed Brand Authorization**\n\nThe Application operates and uses the relevant VEO name and brand elements on the basis of a signed Brand Name and Trademark Authorization Agreement dated 22 September 2026 between Google LLC and Ethan Martin. All ownership rights in Google LLC trademarks and brand assets remain with Google LLC. The authorization governs permitted brand use and does not transfer ownership of those marks.\n\nThe signed brand authorization concerns permitted use of the relevant name and brand elements. Privacy responsibility for the Application and the data-handling practices described in this Policy remains with Ethan Martin, except for processing independently performed by third-party service providers under their own terms and privacy notices.\n\n## Local Storage\n\nThe App stores its own creation history and media locally on your device. Chat threads and their context are maintained locally using on-device storage, and Prompt Builder history is also stored locally. Generated images and videos in the App’s library are stored on the device. We do not upload these local libraries to a developer-operated backend.\n\nLocal-only storage does not mean that content is never transmitted. When you request an AI feature, the inputs required for that request are sent to the relevant AI provider for processing, as described below.\n\n## AI Processing\n\nTo provide requested AI functionality, the App sends relevant content to AI service providers. In the current version, OpenAI is used for text-based assistance and image generation, and MiniMax is used for video generation. Depending on the feature, transmitted data may include text prompts, images, and chat context. The provider returns the requested result to the App.\n\nThe AI providers process requests under their own documentation, terms, privacy notices, retention practices, and safety policies. We do not promise that a provider never retains request data, technical metadata, or generated results. You should avoid submitting information you do not want processed by the provider required for the feature.\n\n## How We Use Information\n\nInformation is processed only as reasonably necessary to:\n\n- perform the AI generation, chat, prompt-building, or media feature you request;\n- maintain local history and library functionality on your device;\n- save or share content when you direct the App to do so;\n- manage subscription access and entitlement status;\n- maintain security, prevent misuse, and comply with applicable legal obligations.\n\n## Subscriptions and Apphud\n\nPaid access is currently offered through subscriptions processed by Apple’s in-app purchase system. The App uses Apphud in a standard subscription-management configuration to help determine purchase and entitlement status. Apphud may process purchase or subscription metadata and an app-scoped or anonymous identifier necessary to provide that functionality. We do not receive or store your full payment-card details.\n\nApple and Apphud process purchase-related information under their own privacy notices and platform rules.\n\n## Device Permissions\n\n### Camera\n\nCamera access may be requested so you can take a photo to attach to an AI conversation or use as source material for animation or video generation.\n\n### Photo Library - Read\n\nPhoto access may be requested so you can choose an existing image for AI chat or image-to-video generation.\n\n### Photo Library - Add Only\n\nAdd-only photo-library access may be used when you choose to save generated media to your photo library. Saving is initiated by you.\n\n### Notifications\n\nThe operating system may present a notification permission request. The current version does not send push notifications or local notifications and does not use notification functionality to collect personal data.\n\nYou can change device permissions at any time in system settings. Disabling a permission may prevent the related feature from working.\n\n## Sharing and Export\n\nYou can export generated content through the system share sheet to apps and services you select, including compatible messaging, storage, AirDrop, and other destinations available on your device. You can also save generated media to Photos. When you choose an external destination, that third party receives the content at your direction and processes it under its own privacy practices.\n\nA separate “Share with friends” option may share the App Store link rather than your generated content.\n\n## Analytics, Advertising, and Diagnostics\n\nThe current version does not use Firebase, third-party analytics, advertising SDKs, or third-party crash-reporting or diagnostics services. We do not use the App to build advertising profiles or collect an advertising identifier for targeted advertising.\n\n## Retention and Deletion\n\nChat threads and Prompt Builder history remain locally on the device until you delete them using available in-app controls or until the relevant local app data is removed. Generated media stored in the App’s local library remains on the device as part of the App’s local data. Other locally stored application data can be removed by deleting the App and its local data from the device.\n\nMedia you separately save to Photos, Files, or another app is controlled by that destination and is not deleted merely because you remove a local chat thread, Prompt Builder entry, or the App itself. AI providers may retain or process request data according to their own policies and legal obligations.\n\n## Data Disclosure\n\nWe do not sell your personal information. Information may be disclosed only as necessary to provide a feature you request, to service providers supporting that feature, to comply with law or valid legal process, or to protect rights, security, and the integrity of the App. User-directed sharing is treated as disclosure at your instruction.\n\n## Security\n\nWe use reasonable technical and organizational measures appropriate to the App’s local-storage design and limited service integrations. No method of electronic storage or transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure. You are responsible for maintaining appropriate security on your device and for deciding what content to submit to external AI services.\n\n## Children and Age\n\nThe App is intended for users aged 16 and older and is not directed to children under 16. We do not knowingly operate an account system or intentionally collect personal information from children under 16. If applicable law requires a higher minimum age or parental consent, those requirements apply.\n\n## International Processing\n\nThird-party AI, purchase, subscription-management, and sharing services may process information in countries other than the country where you live. Their processing is governed by their own terms, privacy notices, and applicable data-protection requirements.\n\n## Third-Party Privacy Practices\n\nThis Privacy Policy describes the Application’s practices. It does not replace the privacy policies of Apple, OpenAI, MiniMax, Apphud, or any other destination or service you choose to use. You should review the relevant third-party documentation if you want more information about their independent processing.\n\n## Changes to This Privacy Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy when features, service providers, legal requirements, or data-handling practices change. The effective date shown at the top identifies the current version. Material changes will be reflected in an updated policy made available with the App or through an appropriate distribution channel.\n\n## Contact\n\nFor privacy questions or requests concerning the Application, contact:\n\nEthan Martin\n9912 Huntingdon Ln\nSt. Louis, MO 63123\nUnited States\nEmail: ethanmartin95@hotmail.com";

const TERMS = "**Effective Date: November 16, 2026**\n\n**Operator**\n\nEthan Martin\n\n**Support**\n\nethanmartin95@hotmail.com\n\n## Acceptance of These Terms\n\nThese Terms of Use (the “Terms”) govern your access to and use of the mobile application (the “App” or the “Application”) operated by Ethan Martin (“we,” “us,” or “our”). By downloading, accessing, purchasing through, or using the App, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the App.\n\nThe App provides AI-assisted tools for creating videos from text and images, building and refining prompts, generating images, maintaining local creation history, and sharing or exporting results.\n\n## Eligibility\n\nThe App is intended for users aged 16 and older. If the law where you live requires a higher age or parental or guardian consent to use services of this type, you must satisfy those requirements before using the App. You may not use the App where use is prohibited by applicable law.\n\n## Brand Name and Trademark Authorization\n\n**Signed Brand Authorization**\n\nThe Application operates and uses the relevant VEO name and brand elements on the basis of a signed Brand Name and Trademark Authorization Agreement dated 22 September 2026 between Google LLC and Ethan Martin. All ownership rights in Google LLC trademarks and brand assets remain with Google LLC. The authorization governs permitted brand use and does not transfer ownership of those marks.\n\nThe App is independently operated by Ethan Martin. References to authorized brand use should not be understood as transferring responsibility for operation of the App, subscriptions, user support, or the App’s separate third-party AI processing services to Google LLC.\n\n## AI Features and Generated Content\n\nThe App may process text prompts, images, and conversation context through external AI service providers to perform the feature you request. AI features may include text assistance, prompt building, image generation, text-to-video generation, image-to-video generation, and the ability to reuse an image generated in a chat as an input for animation or video generation.\n\nAI-generated results are probabilistic and may be inaccurate, incomplete, unexpected, or unsuitable for a particular purpose. You are responsible for reviewing generated content before using, publishing, distributing, or relying on it. We do not guarantee that any prompt will produce a particular result or that a result will be unique.\n\n## Your Inputs and Your Responsibilities\n\nYou retain your rights in prompts, photographs, images, and other materials you submit to the App (“User Content”), subject to rights held by other persons. You grant us and the AI service providers used for your request the limited rights necessary to transmit, process, transform, and return that content solely for providing the requested functionality and operating the service.\n\nYou must have the rights and permissions necessary to use any material you submit. You must not use the App to infringe copyright, trademark, privacy, publicity, personality, or other rights of another person, or to create or distribute unlawful, deceptive, abusive, exploitative, or otherwise prohibited material.\n\n## Prohibited Use\n\nYou may not use the App to:\n\n- create, request, upload, or distribute pornography, sexual exploitation material, or other prohibited sexual content;\n- create or facilitate content involving sexual exploitation or abuse of minors;\n- impersonate another person in a deceptive or unlawful manner, or create misleading content intended to defraud or cause harm;\n- upload content you do not have permission to use;\n- interfere with the App, bypass technical restrictions, probe security, or misuse service credentials or APIs;\n- use generated content in a manner that violates applicable law or the rights of others.\n\n## Local Storage and User Controls\n\nThe App stores its creation history and media locally on your device unless content must be sent to an AI provider to perform a requested generation or you choose to share or export it. Chat threads and Prompt Builder history may be deleted using the available in-app controls. Other locally stored application data is removed when the App and its local data are removed from the device, subject to any copies you separately saved to Photos, Files, another app, or another destination.\n\n## Subscriptions and Purchases\n\nThe current version of the App offers subscription-based access to paid features. Purchases are processed through Apple’s in-app purchase system. Subscription availability, price, billing period, and any applicable introductory terms are shown in the purchase interface before you confirm a transaction.\n\nSubscriptions may renew automatically unless cancelled through your Apple Account settings in accordance with Apple’s rules. We do not directly process your payment card details. Subscription status may be supported by Apphud as a subscription-management service. Refund requests are handled under Apple’s applicable purchase and refund policies.\n\nAdditional purchase types or monetization options may be introduced in future versions. Any such options will be presented in the App with the terms applicable at the time they are offered.\n\n## Device Permissions\n\nDepending on the feature you choose, the App may request access to the camera, selected photos or photo library, and permission to add generated media to your photo library. These permissions are used only to enable the corresponding feature, such as attaching an image, taking a source photo, using an image for generation, or saving generated media. A notification permission request may also be presented by the system; the current version does not send push or local notifications.\n\n## Sharing and Export\n\nYou may choose to save generated media to your photo library or share it through the system share sheet to other apps or services. Once you direct content to another app, platform, person, or service, that destination’s terms and privacy practices apply. The App may also provide a separate option to share a link to the App Store listing.\n\n## Third-Party Services\n\nCertain functions depend on third-party services, including AI processing, Apple in-app purchases, subscription management, and destinations selected through the system share sheet. Those services operate under their own terms, privacy notices, technical limitations, availability, and content policies. We are not responsible for a third party’s independent processing, service interruption, or policy decisions.\n\n## Intellectual Property\n\nExcept for User Content, third-party content, and third-party trademarks, the App, its interface, software, original text, design elements, and related materials are protected by applicable intellectual property laws. These Terms give you a personal, limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable right to use the App for its intended purposes. No other rights are granted.\n\nThird-party names, marks, and brand assets remain the property of their respective owners. Authorized use of VEO-related branding is governed by the signed agreement described in Section 3.\n\n## Availability, Changes, and Termination\n\nWe may update, modify, add, suspend, or remove features to maintain, improve, secure, or develop the App, subject to applicable law. AI providers may also change models, availability, limits, or policies. We may restrict or terminate access where reasonably necessary to address misuse, security concerns, legal requirements, or violations of these Terms.\n\n## Disclaimer of Warranties\n\nTo the maximum extent permitted by law, the App and AI-generated content are provided on an “as is” and “as available” basis. We do not warrant uninterrupted operation, error-free generation, permanent availability of any AI model or third-party service, or that generated content will be accurate, unique, lawful for every intended use, or fit for a particular purpose. Nothing in these Terms excludes warranties or consumer rights that cannot lawfully be excluded.\n\n## Limitation of Liability\n\nTo the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Ethan Martin will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for loss of profits, data, goodwill, opportunity, or business arising from use of or inability to use the App, AI-generated content, or third-party services. Where liability cannot be excluded, it will be limited only to the extent permitted by law. Mandatory consumer rights remain unaffected.\n\n## Indemnity\n\nTo the extent permitted by law, you agree to be responsible for claims, losses, and reasonable costs resulting from your unlawful use of the App, your User Content, or your violation of another person’s rights or these Terms. This provision does not apply where prohibited by consumer law.\n\n## Apple App Store Terms\n\nIf you obtained the App through Apple’s App Store, you acknowledge that these Terms are between you and Ethan Martin, not Apple. Apple is not responsible for the App or its content, except as required by applicable App Store rules or law. Apple and its subsidiaries are intended third-party beneficiaries of these Terms with respect to your license to use the App, and may enforce the relevant provisions against you. Your use of the App must also comply with applicable App Store terms.\n\n## Governing Law\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Missouri, United States, without regard to conflict-of-law principles, except to the extent mandatory consumer law in your country or state provides otherwise. Nothing in these Terms limits rights that cannot be waived under applicable consumer protection law.\n\n## Changes to These Terms\n\nWe may update these Terms when the App, applicable law, third-party services, or our practices change. The effective date at the top of this document identifies the current version. Continued use after an updated version becomes effective constitutes acceptance where permitted by law.\n\n## Contact\n\nQuestions about these Terms or the App may be sent to:\n\nEthan Martin\n9912 Huntingdon Ln\nSt. Louis, MO 63123\nUnited States\nEmail: ethanmartin95@hotmail.com";

